{"surah": 100, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "وَٱلْعَٰدِيَٰتِ ضَبْحًا ", "translation": "By the racers, panting,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلْعَٰدِيَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰyِdَٰʿعْlٱَw", "root": "عدو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ضَبْحًا", "translit": "āًḥْbَḍ", "root": "ضبح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "فَٱلْمُورِيَٰتِ قَدْحًا ", "translation": "And the producers of sparks [when] striking[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱلْمُورِيَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰyِrwُmْlٱَf", "root": "وري"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَدْحًا", "translit": "āًḥْdَq", "root": "قدح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "فَٱلْمُغِيرَٰتِ صُبْحًا ", "translation": "And the chargers at dawn,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱلْمُغِيرَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰryِغُmْlٱَf", "root": "غير"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "صُبْحًا", "translit": "āًḥْbُṣ", "root": "صبح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "فَأَثَرْنَ بِهِۦ نَقْعًا ", "translation": "Stirring up thereby [clouds of] dust,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَثَرْنَ", "translit": "َnْrَhtَaʾَf", "root": "ثور"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَقْعًا", "translit": "āًʿعْqَn", "root": "نقع"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "فَوَسَطْنَ بِهِۦ جَمْعًا ", "translation": "Arriving thereby in the center[1] collectively,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَوَسَطْنَ", "translit": "َnْṭَsَwَf", "root": "وسط"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "جَمْعًا", "translit": "āًʿعْmَjg", "root": "جمع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "إِنَّ ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ لِرَبِّهِۦ لَكَنُودٌ ", "translation": "Indeed mankind, to his Lord, is ungrateful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ", "translit": "َnَٰsnِiʾْlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِرَبِّهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِّbَrِl", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَكَنُودٌ", "translit": "ٌdwُnَkَl", "root": "كند"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "وَإِنَّهُۥ عَلَىٰ ذَٰلِكَ لَشَهِيدٌ ", "translation": "And indeed, he is to that a witness.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَشَهِيدٌ", "translit": "ٌdyِhَhsَl", "root": "شهد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "وَإِنَّهُۥ لِحُبِّ ٱلْخَيْرِ لَشَدِيدٌ ", "translation": "And indeed he is, in love of wealth, intense.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِحُبِّ", "translit": "ِّbُḥِl", "root": "حبب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْخَيْرِ", "translit": "ِrْyَhkْlٱ", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَشَدِيدٌ", "translit": "ٌdyِdَhsَl", "root": "شدد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "أَفَلَا يَعْلَمُ إِذَا بُعْثِرَ مَا فِى ٱلْقُبُورِ ", "translation": "But does he not know that when the contents of the graves are scattered", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفَلَا", "translit": "āَlَfَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بُعْثِرَ", "translit": "َrِhtْʿعُb", "root": "بعثر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْقُبُورِ", "translit": "ِrwُbُqْlٱ", "root": "قبر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "وَحُصِّلَ مَا فِى ٱلصُّدُورِ ", "translation": "And that within the breasts is obtained,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَحُصِّلَ", "translit": "َlِّṣُḥَw", "root": "حصل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلصُّدُورِ", "translit": "ِrwُdُّṣlٱ", "root": "صدر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "إِنَّ رَبَّهُم بِهِمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ لَّخَبِيرٌۢ ", "translation": "Indeed, their Lord with them, that Day, is [fully] Aware.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبَّهُم", "translit": "mُhَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَوْمَئِذٍ", "translit": "ٍhdِyʾَmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَّخَبِيرٌۢ", "translit": "ٌۢryِbَhkَّl", "root": "خبر"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"4": [{"arabic": "والروح أيضا ورد في القرآن على معان كثيرة فلا نطول بإيرادها وكذلك قد يقع الأبهام في الحروف مثل قوله عز وجل ﴿ فأثرن به نقعا فوسطن به جمعا ﴾ {} فالهاء الأولى كناية عن الحوافر وهي الموريات أي أثرن بالحوافر نقعا. والثانية كناية عن الإغارة وهي المغيرات صبحا فوسطن به جمعا جمع المشركون فأغاروا بجمعهم", "english": "And the Spirit (Ruh) also comes in the Quran with many meanings, so we will not prolong by mentioning them. Likewise, ambiguity may occur in the letters, like His saying, the Mighty and Majestic: 'So they raise with it dust, then penetrate with it the gathering' (Quran 100:4-5). The first 'it' (hi) is a metaphor for the hooves, and they are the ones that kindle (al-muriyat), meaning they raise with the hooves dust. And the second 'it' (hi) is a metaphor for the raid, and they are the raiders at dawn (al-mughirat subhan), so they penetrate with it the gathering, the gathering of the polytheists, and they raided with their gathering.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-8.doc.txt", "book_title": "Etiquette of Quran Recitation", "content_type": "dhikr", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the virtue and practice of remembering God, from 'Etiquette of Quran Recitation'", "badge": "Dhikr"}], "10": [{"arabic": "فكيف بكم لو عاينتم الأمور وبعثرت القبور وحصل ما في الصدور وأوقفتم للتحصيل بين يدي الملك الجليل فطارت القلوب لإشفاقها من سالف الذنوب وهتكت عنكم الحجب والأستار وظهرت منكم العيوب والأسرار؟ هنالك تجزى كل نفس بما كسبت إن الله عز وجل يقول \"ليجزى الذي أساءوا بما عملوا ويجزى الذي أحسنوا بالحسنى\" وقال تعالى \"ووضع الكتاب فترى المجرمين مشفقين مما فيه\" الآية جعلنا الله وإياكم عاملين بكتابة متبعين لأوليائه حتى يحلنا وإياكم دار المقامة من فضله إنه حميد مجيد.", "english": "So how would you be if you witnessed the matters and the graves were overturned and what is in the chests (Sudur) was extracted and you were stopped for the accounting before the Majestic King (Al-Malik Al-Jalil), and the hearts (Qulub) flew from their fear of past sins, and the veils (Hujub) and curtains (Astār) were torn from you, and your faults (ʿUyūb) and secrets (Asrār) appeared? There, every soul (Nafs) will be recompensed for what it earned. Indeed, Allah, the Exalted and Majestic, says: \"That He may recompense those who did evil with what they did, and recompense those who did good with the best reward\" (Quran 53:31), and He, the Exalted, says: \"And the Record will be placed, and you will see the criminals fearful of what is in it\" (Quran 83:20). May Allah make us and you doers of His Book, followers of His allies, until He settles us and you in the Abode of Permanence (Dār al-Maqāmah) from His bounty. Indeed, He is Praiseworthy, Glorious.", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book-6a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Condemnation of the World", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Condemnation of the World'", "badge": "Insight"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 250, 2177], [2, 2177, 3286]], "2": [[1, 250, 2146], [2, 2146, 3208]], "3": [[1, 250, 2111], [2, 2111, 3260]], "4": [[1, 250, 1593], [2, 1593, 2074], [3, 2074, 3417]], "5": [[1, 250, 1662], [2, 1662, 2093], [3, 2093, 3182]], "6": [[1, 350, 1442], [2, 1442, 3314], [3, 3314, 4705], [4, 4705, 6349]], "7": [[1, 350, 1872], [2, 1872, 3029], [3, 3029, 3975], [4, 3975, 5383]], "8": [[1, 350, 1727], [2, 1727, 2603], [3, 2603, 3719], [4, 3719, 5017]], "9": [[1, 350, 1210], [2, 1210, 2053], [3, 2053, 2752], [4, 275